# Comprehensive README: AI-Powered Historical Podcast Generator Azure Function

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the AI-Powered Historical Podcast Generator, an Azure Function application designed to automate the creation of short, witty, and insightful historical podcast episodes. The system orchestrates several cloud services, including Azure OpenAI for script generation, Azure Cognitive Services for Text-to-Speech (TTS), Azure Blob Storage for audio hosting, Azure Queue Storage for decoupled processing, and Azure Cosmos DB for data persistence.

The architecture is designed for **scalability**, **decoupling**, and **asynchronous processing** to ensure a fast user experience while handling resource-intensive tasks in the background.

---

## 1. Architecture and Workflow Overview

The application follows a two-stage, event-driven architecture, initiated by an HTTP request and completed by a Queue-triggered function.

### 1.1. High-Level Diagram

| Component | Role | Technologies |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Orchestrator** (`orchestrator`) | **Front-end API (HTTP Trigger)**. Receives user request, generates script, creates audio, and enqueues a message for background processing. | Azure Function (HTTP Trigger), Azure OpenAI, Azure Cognitive Services (TTS), Azure Blob Storage, Azure Queue Storage |
| **Queue** (`myqueuename`) | **Decoupling Mechanism**. Stores metadata for the next step, ensuring the HTTP function can return quickly. | Azure Queue Storage |
| **Writer** (`eventCosmosWriter`) | **Back-end Processor (Queue Trigger)**. Persists the event data to Cosmos DB, extracts addresses from the script, geocodes them, and updates the database. | Azure Function (Queue Trigger), Azure Cosmos DB, Google Geocoding API, Azure OpenAI |

### 1.2. Detailed Workflow

1.  **Request Ingestion**: A client sends a `POST` request to the `orchestrator` function with event details (`eventName`, `town`, `country`, etc.).
2.  **Script Generation**: The `orchestrator` calls the **Azure OpenAI Assistants API** to generate a full podcast script featuring two hosts, "Elijah" and "Ayana."
3.  **Audio Generation**: The script is passed to the **Azure Cognitive Services TTS API**. The script is parsed to identify dialogue segments and assign distinct voices (Andrew and Emma) using SSML.
4.  **Audio Upload**: The generated MP3 audio file is uploaded to **Azure Blob Storage** (`podcasts-audio` container) with a **Shared Access Signature (SAS)** token for read-only access, ensuring the audio URL is secure and temporary (30-day expiry).
5.  **Queue Message**: A JSON message containing the event metadata, including the audio URL, is prepared. The message uses the `town` as the document `id` and the `country` as the `partitionKey` for Cosmos DB.
6.  **Fast Response**: The message is sent to the `myqueuename` queue **without awaiting completion**, allowing the `orchestrator` function to immediately return a `200 OK` response to the user with the generated script and audio URL.
7.  **Background Processing**: The `eventCosmosWriter` function is triggered by the new message in the queue.
8.  **Cosmos DB Upsert**: The function attempts to patch the new event into an existing document (identified by `town`/`country`). If the document or the `events` array does not exist, it is created.
9.  **Address Extraction**: The script text is sent back to the **Azure OpenAI Assistants API** with a prompt to extract specific, mappable street-level addresses mentioned in the dialogue.
10. **Geocoding**: The extracted addresses are geocoded using the **Google Geocoding API** to obtain latitude and longitude coordinates.
11. **Cosmos DB Patch**: The geocoded address data is patched back into the corresponding event entry in the Cosmos DB document.

---

## 2. Function Reference

### 2.1. `orchestrator` (HTTP Trigger)

| Property | Value/Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Trigger** | HTTP (POST) |
| **Endpoint** | `/api/orchestrator` |
| **Input Body** | JSON: `{ eventName, eventYears, eventCategory, town, country }` |
| **Output** | JSON: `{ event, script, audioUrl }` |
| **Key Dependencies** | `generateScriptFromEvent`, `textToSpeech`, `@azure/storage-queue` |
| **Cosmos DB Strategy** | Uses `town` as `id` and `country` as `partitionKey`. |

### 2.2. `eventCosmosWriter` (Queue Trigger)

| Property | Value/Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Trigger** | Azure Queue Storage |
| **Queue Name** | `myqueuename` |
| **Connection** | `AzureWebJobsStorage` |
| **Key Dependencies** | `patchNewEvent`, `getEventIndex`, `extractAddresses`, `geocodeAll`, `patchAddresses` |
| **Purpose** | Decoupled, idempotent persistence and enrichment of event data. |

### 2.3. Utility Functions (`src/utils`)

| Utility File | Description | External Dependency |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `openaiClient.js` | Initializes the client for **Azure OpenAI Service** using the Assistants API. | Azure OpenAI |
| `generateScriptFromEvent.js` | Sends a detailed prompt to the Assistant to generate the podcast script. | Azure OpenAI |
| `textToSpeech.js` | Parses the script, generates SSML with two distinct voices (Andrew and Emma), and calls the **Azure Cognitive Services Text-to-Speech API**. | Azure Cognitive Services TTS |
| `blobStorage.js` | Uploads the generated audio buffer to the `podcasts-audio` container and generates a read-only, time-limited **SAS URL** (30 days). | Azure Blob Storage |
| `patchNewEvent.js` | Handles the complex upsert logic for Cosmos DB: attempts to patch an event into an existing document, or creates the array/document if missing. | Azure Cosmos DB |
| `extractAddresses.js` | Uses a targeted prompt with the Azure OpenAI Assistant to identify and extract mappable locations from the script text. | Azure OpenAI |
| `geocodeAddress.js` | Calls the **Google Geocoding API** to resolve a single address string into a latitude/longitude coordinate pair. | Google Geocoding API |
| `geocodeAll.js` | Orchestrates the geocoding of all extracted addresses. | Google Geocoding API |
| `getEvents.js` | **Data Retrieval API (HTTP Trigger)**. Retrieves a list of historical events for a given `location` and `country` by calling `getEventsForLocation.js`. | Azure OpenAI (for event list generation) |
| `getEventsForLocation.js` | **(Misleading Name)** This function does **not** query Cosmos DB. It uses the **Azure OpenAI Assistants API** to *generate* a list of historical events for a given location and country. | Azure OpenAI |

---

## 3. Configuration and Environment Variables

The function relies heavily on environment variables for connecting to various cloud services. These must be configured in your `local.settings.json` file during local development and in the Azure Function App configuration settings for deployment.

| Variable Name | Service | Description | Example Value |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `AzureWebJobsStorage` | Azure Storage | Connection string for the Storage Account used by the Function App, specifically for the queue (`myqueuename`). | `DefaultEndpointsProtocol=...` |
| `COSMOS_DB_ENDPOINT` | Azure Cosmos DB | The URI endpoint for your Cosmos DB account. | `https://[account-name].documents.azure.com:443/` |
| `COSMOS_DB_KEY` | Azure Cosmos DB | The primary or secondary key for your Cosmos DB account. | `[Your-Cosmos-Key]` |
| `BLOB_CONNECTION_STRING` | Azure Blob Storage | Connection string for the Storage Account hosting the `podcasts-audio` container. | `DefaultEndpointsProtocol=...` |
| `AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT` | Azure OpenAI | The base URL for your Azure OpenAI service instance. | `https://[resource-name].openai.azure.com/` |
| `AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY` | Azure OpenAI | The API key for your Azure OpenAI service instance. | `[Your-AOAI-Key]` |
| `OPENAI_ASSISTANT_ID` | Azure OpenAI | The ID of the pre-configured Assistant used for script and address generation. | `asst_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx` |
| `TTS_ENDPOINT` | Azure Cognitive Services | The endpoint for the Text-to-Speech service. | `https://[region].tts.speech.microsoft.com/cognitiveservices/v1` |
| `TTS_KEY` | Azure Cognitive Services | The subscription key for the Text-to-Speech service. | `[Your-TTS-Key]` |
| `GOOGLE_GEOCODING_API_KEY` | Google Maps Platform | The API key for accessing the Google Geocoding Service. | `AIzaSy...` |

